                                              interfaces in java 
          
          1. interface start with the interface keyword (before 8)
          2. interface method are by default public and abstract
          3. interface are used for full abstraction( partial abstraction)
          4. interface dose not have constructor and you cannot create the object


                             interfaces are use to resolve the  diamond problem in java


    resolution of diamond problem
    
    u can implement multiple interfaces on a single class if that interfaces are not having same default methods  (same signature) then a 
    child class will not be concern about the ambiguity problem because both the interfaces is going to content the methods without implementation 
    so you can really implement any method from the above interfaces



   
